Row 3, column 2 is the create modal's **Name field's HELP line** ("the
display name; also the source of the session's tmux slug"), rendered in the
`dimmed` token per SPEC.md:1355/1357's own requirement that a dialog's
"explanatory help" render `dimmed` -- NOT the cwd ghost (which is correctly
absent in this scenario's 3-way-ambiguous case: the ambiguous-match
requirement 15 ghosts nothing). The old whole-grid assertion cannot
distinguish "the modal is themed as SPEC requires" from "a ghost leaked
somewhere unexpected"; narrowing the scan to the cwd field's own rows is the
only way to keep testing the ghost specifically once every field's help line
is dimmed too, which is exactly what `cdb927b`/`adb7db4` did and what the
current, narrowed `clientCWDFieldShowsNoGhostText` still does.
